UPDATE public.profiles
SET gospel_data = '[{"title":"The Roles of the Husband: A Biblical Perspective","linkUrl":"https://crosspointechurchmn.snappages.site/media/8z7hwh6/roles-of-the-husband","section":"1","subsections":[{"title":"Introduction:","content":"","questions":[],"nestedSubsections":[{"title":"Role One: The Role of the Husband is to be a Leader.","content":"<p>Ephesians 5:23 For the husband is the head of the wife, as Christ also is the head of the church, He Himself being the savior of the body. <br>1 Corinthians 11:3 But I want you to understand that the head of every man is Christ, the head of a woman is her husband, and the head of Christ is God. </p><ol><li><p>Biblical leadership is characterized by servanthood. <br>Matthew 20:25-28 But Jesus called them to Himself and said, “You know that the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and their great men exercise authority over them. It is not this way among you, but whoever wishes to become great among you shall be your servant, and whoever wishes to be first among you shall be your slave; just as the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give His life a ransom for many.” </p><ol><li><p>Jesus is the head of the church. He is our Lord, and yet He does not lord it over us. He came into this world, not to be served, but to serve, and to give His life as a ransom for many. </p></li><li><p>Jesus Christ sets the example for leadership. <br>John 13:3-15 Jesus, knowing that the Father had given all things into His hands, and that He had come forth from God and was going back to God, got up from supper, and laid aside His garments; taking a towel, He girded Himself. <br>Then He poured water into the basin, and began to wash the disciples’ feet and to wipe them with the towel with which He was girded. So He came to Simon Peter. He said to Him, “Lord, do You wash my feet?” Jesus answered and said to him, “What I do you do not realize now, but you will understand hereafter.” Peter said to Him, “Never shall You wash my feet!” Jesus answered him, “If I do not wash you, you have no part with me.” <br>Simon Peter said to Him, “Lord, then wash not only my feet, but also my hands and my head.” Jesus said to him, “He who has bathed needs only wash his feet, but is completely clean; and you are clean, but not all of you.” For He knew the one who was betraying Him; for this reason He said, “Not all of you are clean.” <br>So when He had washed their feet, and taken His garments and reclined at the table again, He said to them, “Do you know what I have done to you? You call Me Teacher and Lord; and you are right, for so I am. If I then, the Lord and the Teacher, washed your feet, you also ought to wash one another’s feet. For I gave you an example that you also should do as I did to you.” </p></li><li><p>Jesus is indeed the Head of the church, for the sake of the church. <br>Ephesians 1:22 And God has put all things under the authority of Christ, and he gave him this authority for the benefit of the church. </p></li><li><p>Wayne Mack states, “The husband is to live for the sake of his wife always keeping her best interests at heart.”<sup>1 </sup></p></li><li><p>When a husband uses his headship for his own selfish benefit, he is not following the example of Christ. Rather, he is abusing the authority that was given to him. </p></li></ol></li><li><p>How can a husband lead biblically? </p><ol><li><p>A husband must spend a great deal of time with his wife. <br>Mark 1:17 And Jesus said to them, “Follow me, and I will make you become fishers of men.” </p><ol><li><p>Jesus did not use distance learning with his disciples. Instead, he walked and talked with them daily! </p></li><li><p>Husbands, as leaders, you are the ones responsible to make sure that you spend an adequate amount of time with your wife. </p><ol><li><p>Husbands must also work and provide for his wife and family. This will take a great deal of time, but it’s the husband’s responsibility to ensure that time is dedicated for his wife and family. <br>1 Timothy 5:8 But if anyone does not provide for his own, and especially for those of his household, he has denied the faith and is worse than an unbeliever. </p></li><li><p>Husbands should identify activities that involve their wife, even if that means giving up some cherished activities. </p></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p>A husband must instruct his wife. <br>Matthew 5:1-2 When Jesus saw the crowds, He went up on the mountain; and after He sat down, His disciples came to Him. He opened His mouth and began to teach them, . . . <br>1 Corinthians 14:35 If they desire to learn anything, let them ask their own husbands at home; for it is improper for a woman to speak in church. </p><ol><li><p>Husbands, you are called to instruct your wife. Therefore, you must be well-grounded in the bible. </p><ol><li><p>Husbands, like all mankind, need to be always learning and growing in God’s word. </p></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p>A husband must be a good example. <br>Luke 9:23 And He was saying to them all, “If anyone wishes to come after Me, he must deny himself, and take up his cross daily and follow me. <br>John 13:15 For I gave you an example that you also should do as I did to you. </p><ol><li><p>Jesus lived a life, exemplifying exactly how we are to live, if we would live a life pleasing to God. </p></li><li><p>Our wives should be able to see our conduct, words, tones, gestures, and over all manner of life as exemplary examples for them to imitate. <br>Philippians 3:17 Brethren, join in following my example, and observe those who walk according to the pattern you have in us. </p></li><li><p>Husbands, you are not perfect, but you should strive hard to be worthy of being followed. </p><ol><li><p>Husbands should: </p><ol><li><p>Pray </p></li><li><p>Read their Bible daily </p></li><li><p>Confess their sins and shortcomings </p></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"Role Two: The Role of the Husband is to be a Lover.","content":"<p>1 Corinthians 13:4-8 Love is patient, love is kind and is not jealous; love does not brag and is not arrogant, does not act unbecomingly; it does not seek its own, is not provoked, does not take into account a wrong suffered, does not rejoice in unrighteousness, but rejoices with the truth; bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, endures all things. Love never fails. </p><ol><li><p>Aspects of biblical love. </p><ol><li><p>Biblical love is an act of the will, not based upon our feelings. </p><ol><li><p>Husbands must be determined to love their wives at all times, as an act of the will. </p></li><li><p>Biblical love is first concerned with pleasing God, and then benefitting the loved one 2 Corinthians 5:9. <br>Ephesians 5:25 Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ also loved the church and gave Himself up for her, </p></li></ol></li><li><p>Biblical love is other-centered. </p><ol><li><p>Francis Foulkes teaches, “Love that is totally unselfish, that seeks not its own satisfaction, nor even affection answering affection, but that strives for the highest good of the one loved.”<sup>2</sup> </p></li><li><p>Dr Stuart Scott states, “God’s kind of love is: A selfless and enduring commitment of the will to care about and benefit another person by righteous, truthful, and compassionate thoughts, words, and actions.”<sup>3</sup> </p></li><li><p>A husband that loves in this manner will gladly lay his own interests aside to take care of his wife and will not expect anything in return. <br>John 15:13 Greater love has no one than this, that someone lay down his life for his friends. </p></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p>Practical application for husbands to biblically love their wives. </p><ol><li><p>Husbands must love their wives by taking care of them. <br>Ephesians 5:29 for no one ever hated his own flesh, but nourishes and cherishes it, just as Christ also does the church, </p></li><li><p>Husbands must cherish their wives. </p><ol><li><p>To cherish is to: “Treat as dear; to care for tenderly.”<sup>4</sup> </p></li><li><p>Husbands are responsible for watching over their wife’s health and making sure she is treated and cared for properly. </p></li><li><p>Bruce states, “Just as a man provides for his own comfort and well-being, so he should provide for his wife’s.”<sup>5</sup> </p><ol><li><p>To do this properly, a husband must study and know his wife 1 Peter 3:7.  </p></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p>Husbands are called to love their wife in an extraordinary way. They are to love their wife as much as Christ loved the church, laying down His life for her! <br>Ephesians 5:25 Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ also loved the church and gave Himself up for her. </p><ol><li><p>Christ loves the church unconditionally. <br>Romans 5:8 But God demonstrates His own love toward us, in that while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us. </p></li><li><p>Christ loves us intensely. <br>John 13:1 Now before the Feast of the Passover, Jesus knowing that His hour had come that He would depart out of this world to the Father, having loved His own who were in the world, He love them to the end. </p></li><li><p>Christ’s love for the church will never end! <br>Romans 8:38-39 For I am convinced that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor things present, nor things to come, nor powers, nor height, nor depth, nor any other created thing, will be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord. </p></li><li><p>Christ loves the church unselfishly. <br>Philippians 2:6-7 who, although He existed in the form of God, did not regard equality with God a thing to be grasped, but emptied Himself, taking the form of a bond-servant, and being made in the likeness of men. </p></li><li><p>Christ loves the church sacrificially. <br>1 Peter 2:24 and He Himself bore our sins in His body on the cross, so that we might die to sin and live to righteousness; for by His wounds you were healed. <br>1 Peter 3:18 For Christ also died for sins once for all, the just for the unjust, so that He might bring us to God, having been put to death in the flesh, but made alive in the spirit; </p></li><li><p>Husbands are instructed to love their wife as Christ loved the church. This means they are to love their wife unconditionally, intensely, unendingly, unselfishly, and sacrificially. </p></li></ol></li><li><p>Can a husband actually love his wife in these ways? </p><ol><li><p>Husbands need to realize that loving, nourishing, and cherishing a wife to the extent God calls them is supernatural and humanly impossible in their own strength. Husbands must rely on the Lord to strengthen them to fulfill what they were called to do.  <br>Philippians 4:13 I can do all things through Him who strengthens me. </p></li><li><p>For a husband to love his wife the way Christ loved the church, he must first know the love of Christ himself. </p></li></ol></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"Role Three: The Role of the Husband is to be a Learner.","content":"<ol><li><p>A Husband must study the Word of God. </p><ol><li><p>Husbands must become diligent in both reading and studying God’s word regularly and faithfully if they would become the husbands God wants them to be. <br>2 Timothy 2:15 Be diligent to present yourself approved to God as a workman who does not need to be ashamed, accurately handling the word of truth. </p></li></ol></li><li><p>A Husband must study his wife. <br>1 Peter 3:7 You husbands in the same way, live with your wives in an understanding way, as with someone weaker, since she is a woman; and show her honor as a fellow heir of the grace of life, so that your prayers will not be hindered. </p><ol><li><p>For a husband to live with his wife in an understanding way, he must gain knowledge about her. He must study her and learn about her comprehensively.</p></li></ol></li></ol><ol><li><p>Wayne A. Mack, Strengthening Your Marriage, 34.</p></li><li><p>Francis Foulkes, Ephesians, Tyndale New Testament Commentaries,165. </p></li><li><p>Stuart Scott, The Exemplary Husband, 106. </p></li><li><p>Emery and Brewster, The New Century Dictionary, s.v. “cherish.” </p></li><li><p>F. F. Bruce, The Epistle to the Ephesians, 391.</p></li></ol><p></p>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]}],"scriptureReferences":[]}],"linkDescription":"Watch the recording of this content."},{"title":"Homework","section":"2","subsections":[{"title":"Homework Questions","content":"<p>Complete the exercises below and save your answers.</p>","questions":[{"id":"q-1762815699165-cmazjtvcl","question":"<p>Memory Verse: </p><p>Ephesians 5:25 Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ also loved the church and gave Himself up for her,</p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:01:39.165Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815727530-636ay6o5j","question":"<p>Scripture: Read Ephesians 5:25-33 with your spouse. </p><p>Discuss what it means to “love their own wives as their own bodies.” Give examples of how you love your own body, and how you should therefore love your wife. </p><p>Discuss what it means to “love your wives, just as Christ also loved the church.” Give examples of how Christ loved the church, and how you therefore should love your wives.</p><p></p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:07.530Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815743329-368lco85v","question":"<p>Review and discuss this lesson with your spouse.</p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:23.329Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815771780-km1fv8sxs","question":"<p>Pray daily to love your wife as much as you love yourself; to love her as Christ loves the church.</p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:51.780Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815788546-a7zpmi1z2","question":"<p>Attend Church together.</p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:03:08.546Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815849312-qrorii0ba","question":"<p>Application</p><ul><li><p>Make a list of 10 things you appreciate about your wife. Tell her!</p></li><li><p>Make a list of 10 ways that you can love your wife “as you love yourself.” Do it!</p></li><li><p>Think of 2 ways you can love your wife sacrificially. Do it!</p></li></ul><p></p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:04:09.312Z","maxLength":2000}],"nestedSubsections":[]}]}]'::jsonb, updated_at = NOW()
WHERE slug = '0dd094bf';
